# 22. RATE LIMIT IMPLEMENTATION

For the first version, use CacheService.

```javascript
function w16CheckRateLimit(
  request,
  context,
  limit
) {

  const cache =
    CacheService.getScriptCache();

  const actorId =
    context.authorization &&
    context.authorization.actor &&
    context.authorization.actor.id
      ? context.authorization.actor.id
      : 'UNKNOWN';

  const minuteKey =
    Math.floor(Date.now() / 60000);

  const key =
    'W16_RATE_' +
    Utilities.base64EncodeWebSafe(
      actorId +
      '|' +
      request.operation +
      '|' +
      minuteKey
    ).substring(0, 180);

  const current =
    Number(cache.get(key) || 0);

  if (current >= limit) {
    return false;
  }

  cache.put(
    key,
    String(current + 1),
    70
  );

  return true;
}
```

Note:

```text
CacheService
≠
permanent quota database
```

For enterprise-grade metering, W16 should eventually maintain durable usage counters.

